Changelog: 14-11-2026 12:36:09

Fixed. An app that changes how the console runs is marked "changes the board", the name its chapter of the wiki
opens with: under its tile, in the tile's popup ("Changes the board."), in the question before it is installed or
opened and in the list of Install all. It said "changes the system".

Changelog: 14-11-2026 12:22:49

Fixed. The portal lists XBOX Remote Play under that name, with XBOX in capitals (apps.toml).

Changelog: 14-11-2026 12:11:51

Fixed. The portal's own update works: until now it failed and left no portal installed. The portal unpacks the new
release inside its own folder and runs its installer from there, and the installer removed that folder, itself
included, before it copied the new portal. The installer now copies the new portal beside the installed one first
and lets it take its place only then. What the portal remembers (the apps it installed and their releases, the
wallpaper and the ones used before, a downloaded update) is in a folder of its own,
~/.local/share/bazzite-console-suite/state, no longer in the program's folder, where every install and update
removed it; an install moves what an earlier portal kept there, once. --uninstall keeps that folder and --purge
removes it. Sys info's first section is Console, with the Mainboard and the Product. The portal's text says the
console where it said the board.

